Education Indicators in Africa (2010–2023)
Exploratory analysis of primary education outcomes using UNESCO data.


Research Questions
What are the trends in attendance & life expectancy (2010–2023)?

What are the gender and urban‑rural gaps?

What is the association between education spending (% GDP) and attendance?

Dataset
7 CSV files from UNESCO, country‑year level (54 African countries, 2010–2023)

Missing values marked #N/B → converted to NA during import

Key indicators: attendance, school life expectancy, expenditure, enrolment, teachers, school‑age population

🔧 Core Variables
Variable	Description
attend_both	Net primary attendance (%)
life_exp_male/female	School life expectancy (years)
exp_prim_gdp	Primary spending (% of GDP)
attend_urban/rural	Urban/rural attendance (%)
gender_gap_life	Derived (male – female years)
urban_rural_gap	Derived (urban – rural pp)

Methods
Descriptive stats, paired t‑tests, correlation

Linear regression (simple + multiple)

Key Findings
Average attendance: ~75% (range: 25–99%)

Life expectancy rose from ~9.0 to ~10.5 years

Gender gap: +0.3 years for males (significant but small)

Urban‑rural gap: +8.5 pp for urban (p < 0.001)

Spending association: +1.5 pp attendance per 1% GDP spent (p = 0.007), controlling for year & urban‑rural gap

Limitations
Observational, no causal claims

Missing data may be non‑random

No country fixed effects or individual controls
